      "spi": { "miso": "D9", "mosi": "D10", "sck": "D8", "ss": "D0" },
      "uart": {
        "hardware": ["D6/D7"],
        "conditionalNote": "D6/D7 map to hardware UART1 TX/RX by default. Enabling \"USB CDC on Boot\" in the board's Tools menu moves the serial console onto native USB and frees D6/D7 as plain GPIO."
      },
      "notes": [
        "Exposes 11 usable GPIO broken out as D0-D10; the remaining ESP32-S3 GPIO are used internally for SPI flash/PSRAM and USB and are not broken out on the XIAO castellated pads.",
        "Has an onboard LiPo charge IC and a JST 1.25mm 2-pin battery connector. Per Seeed's official docs, the negative (BAT-) pad is the one closest to the USB-C port and positive (BAT+) is the pad farthest from it -- do not assume polarity from wire color.",
        "D4/D5 are the default I2C pins (SDA/SCL).",
        "D-to-GPIO mapping (e.g., D6=GPIO43, D7=GPIO44) is approximate and provided for orientation only; verify against the current Seeed wiki before writing low-level/register code."
      ],
      "referenceLinks": [
        "https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/xiao_esp32s3_getting_started/",
        "https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/xiao_esp32s3_battery_usage/"
      ]
    },
